<v Luke Malone>如果治疗师认为某人对孩子构成威胁，根据强制报告法，他们有法律义务将其举报。如果不这么做，他们可能会失去执照。所以当谈到辅导恋童癖者时，治疗师必须衡量那个人采取行动的可能性有多大。他们处于一个棘手的境地，必须就某人有多危险做出判断。

00:45:50.300 --> 00:46:08.190
<v Luke Malone>Professor Elizabeth Letourneau is one of the top researchers on child sexual abuse in the world. She's done this work for 25 years. She says the great thing about mandatory reporting laws are that they've brought to light lots of crimes against children. But as they got more popular, she saw it affect the number of people reaching out for help.
<v Luke Malone>伊丽莎白·勒图诺（Elizabeth Letourneau）教授是世界上研究儿童性虐待的顶级研究员之一。她从事这项工作25年了。她说，强制报告法的伟大之处在于它们揭露了许多针对儿童的罪行。但随着它们变得越来越普遍，她发现这影响了寻求帮助的人数。

00:46:08.190 --> 00:46:19.630
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>Self-referrals for help really dried up. And people watched helplines just go silent, because folks are too afraid to reach out for help. The consequences are too high.
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>主动寻求帮助的人数真的干涸了。人们眼睁睁看着求助热线陷入沉默，因为人们太害怕寻求帮助了。后果太严重了。

00:46:19.630 --> 00:46:41.630
<v Luke Malone>Professor Letourneau is the director of the Moore Center for the Prevention of Child Sexual Abuse at Johns Hopkins University. And it's with that mandate, the prevention of child sexual abuse, that she's pushing hard for research into people like Adam. Amazingly, there's very little research on pedophilia. We don't know much about the sexuality of adolescents, let alone what might make someone a pedophile.
<v Luke Malone>勒图诺教授是约翰霍普金斯大学儿童性虐待预防中心的主任。正是在预防儿童性虐待这一使命的驱使下，她正在大力推动对亚当这类人群的研究。令人惊讶的是，关于恋童癖的研究非常少。我们对青少年的性行为知之甚少，更不用说是什么可能使一个人成为恋童癖者了。

00:46:41.630 --> 00:46:46.020
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>It is a gigantic black hole in science.
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>这是科学中的一个巨大的黑洞。

00:46:46.020 --> 00:47:03.200
<v Luke Malone>Among things we don't know, we don't know that there's a connection between being abused and developing an attraction to kids. Crazy, right? We don't know what's normal, when it comes to the sexual development of children. It might be normal for a 12 year old to be attracted to a six or eight year old.
<v Luke Malone>我们不知道的事情中，包括不知道被虐待和产生对孩子的吸引力之间是否有联系。很疯狂，对吧？当涉及儿童性发育时，我们不知道什么是正常的。12岁的孩子被6或8岁的孩子吸引可能是正常的。

00:47:03.200 --> 00:47:14.940
<v Luke Malone>Another thing that has not been researched in-depth is if having an attraction to kids makes it more dangerous to be around them. On its face, it seems obvious. But there is no evidence to support it.
<v Luke Malone>另一件没有经过深入研究的事情是，是否有对孩子的吸引力会使接近他们变得更危险。从表面上看，这似乎很明显。但没有任何证据支持这一点。

00:47:14.940 --> 00:47:37.370
<v Luke Malone>The research that we do have, and this is from a very small sample size, suggests that pedophiles are more lucky to be shorter, left-handed, and have a lower IQ. Another study says that being knocked unconscious before the age of 13 may be a factor. It shows just how little we've scratched the surface.
<v Luke Malone>我们确实拥有的一些研究（基于很小的样本量）表明，恋童癖者更有可能是个子较矮、左撇子且智商较低。另一项研究称，在13岁之前因撞击失去知觉可能是一个因素。这显示了我们对真相的了解有多浅。

00:47:37.370 --> 00:48:00.940
<v Luke Malone>For years, Letourneau has been trying to change all this, to get money for research, and for prevention programs. But there's not much money for that. Funders don't want to be associated with pedophilia research. The stigma is too great. Even someone like Letourneau, who wants to do this research in order to prevent children from being abused, has been called a pedophile sympathizer, simply for advocating these programs.
<v Luke Malone>多年来，勒图诺一直试图改变这一切，试图为研究和预防项目争取资金。但对此投入的资金并不多。资助者不想与恋童癖研究扯上关系。这种耻辱感太强烈了。甚至像勒图诺这样为了防止儿童被虐待而想要进行研究的人，仅仅因为倡导这些项目就被称为“恋童癖同情者”。

00:48:00.940 --> 00:48:19.700
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>If we can prevent this, we can prevent a lot of harm and a lot of cost. And we just don't. It's nuanced. It's difficult to wrap your head around. It's a lot easier to say these guys are monsters. Let's put them in prison. Let's put them on a registry. Let's put them in civil commitment facilities. And forget about them.
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>如果我们能预防这一点，我们就能防止许多伤害和许多代价。但我们只是不做。这是微妙的。很难理解。说这些人是怪物要容易得多。把他们关进监狱。把他们放进登记处。把他们关进民事收容设施。然后忘掉他们。

00:48:19.700 --> 00:48:41.440
<v Luke Malone>The place that research is most solid is the numbers. Studies suggest that an astonishingly large number of men are pedophiles. A respected survey by Michael Seto, director of the Forensic Research Unit at the University of Ottawa, found that 3% of all men have sexually offended against a prepubescent child. Though not all these men would be considered pedophiles.
<v Luke Malone>研究最坚实的地方是数字。研究表明，数量惊人多的男性是恋童癖者。渥太华大学法医研究部门主任迈克尔·塞托（Michael Seto）的一项权威调查发现，3%的男性曾经对青春期前的儿童进行过性侵犯。尽管并非所有这些男性都会被视为恋童癖者。

00:48:41.440 --> 00:49:10.490
<v Luke Malone>But he goes on to estimate that 1% to 3% of men would meet the diagnostic criteria for pedophilia, which equates to anywhere between 1.2 million and 3.4 million pedophiles in the US alone. That means there are lots of people out there who presumably try not to offend, with nowhere to turn to for help. There's almost no research to explain why they are the way they are, and no known treatment. Which is how a teenager might conclude that his best option is to invent his own way forward.
<v Luke Malone>但他进而估计，1%到3%的男性符合恋童癖的诊断标准，这相当于仅在美国就有120万到340万恋童癖者。这意味着外面有很多人大概正努力不进行侵害，但却无处求助。几乎没有研究来解释他们为什么会这样，也没有已知的治疗方法。这就是为什么一个青少年可能会断定他最好的选择是自己想出一条路。

00:49:10.490 --> 00:49:31.040
<v Luke Malone>At 17, Adam started searching online for other guys like himself, young men struggling to deal with their attraction to kids. And some responded. They got to talking online. And soon there were a bunch of them, communicating on a daily basis. Before long, Adam realized that he had inadvertently formed a support group for young pedophiles.
<v Luke Malone>17岁时，亚当开始在网上寻找像他一样的其他年轻人，那些正在努力应对被孩子吸引的年轻人。有些人回应了。他们在网上交谈。很快就有了不少人，每天都在沟通。没过多久，亚当意识到他无意中形成了一个针对年轻恋童癖者的互助小组。

00:49:31.040 --> 00:50:07.420
<v Luke Malone>There are currently nine members, ranging in age from 16 to 22, eight men and one woman. They communicate in the same way that any bunch of teenagers do-- Gchat, text, email, the odd phone call, or video chat. And there's usually at least a few people online each night. I've talked to five of them, and met three of those in person. They all said they're glad to have found the group. And for most, it's the only outlet they have. Everyone I've spoken to has a story about how the group saved them. A 22-year-old college student told me this one.
<v Luke Malone>目前有9名成员，年龄从16岁到22岁不等，8男1女。他们以任何青少年都会用的方式沟通——Gchat、短信、电子邮件、偶尔的电话或视频聊天。通常每晚至少有几个人在线。我跟其中5个人聊过，亲自见过其中3个。他们都说很高兴找到了这个小组。对大多数人来说，这是他们唯一的出口。我采访过的每个人都有故事讲述这个小组如何拯救了他们。一名22岁的大学生告诉我这个故事。

00:50:07.420 --> 00:50:34.690
<v Anonymous College Student>There was a time when I was really running out of hope for the future. I was unemployed, and I felt like no one was going to give me a shot. And I felt like I had literally no shot in life. And I kind of wanted to kill myself. I didn't do it. The first thing I thought of was especially Adam, in specific, but the rest of them as well, that I couldn't let them down like that.
<v Anonymous College Student>有段时间我真的对未来快要失去希望了。我失业了，我觉得没人会给我一个机会。我觉得我在生活中真的毫无希望。我甚至想自杀。我没做。我首先想到的是亚当，具体说就是他，当然还有其他成员，我不能那样辜负他们。

00:50:34.690 --> 00:50:54.350
<v Luke Malone>The governing principle of the group is that you can only be a part of it if you agree that it's wrong to have sex with kids. There are other pedophile support groups online who feel the opposite, who advocate for the abolishment of age of consent laws. Others suggest that molesting children is wrong because it's illegal, but stop short of taking a moral stand.
<v Luke Malone>小组的准则是，只有当你同意与孩子发生性关系是错误的时候，你才能成为其中的一员。网上还有其他的恋童癖互助小组持相反意见，他们主张废除同意年龄法。其他人则认为猥亵儿童是错的，因为这是非法的，但止步于此，没有采取道德立场。

00:50:54.350 --> 00:51:06.730
<v Luke Malone>Adam's group absolutely takes a moral stand. A few times, he's found himself trying to convince potential members of the group that having sex with children is wrong. And occasionally, Adam has to turn someone away.
<v Luke Malone>亚当的小组确实采取了道德立场。有几次，他发现自己在试图说服小组的潜在成员，与孩子发生性关系是错误的。偶尔，亚当不得不拒绝某些人。

00:51:06.730 --> 00:51:42.720
<v Adam>There was one time someone came in, and he admitted to me pretty much right away that he'd done some sexual things with a five-year-old kid. And right then and there, I said we can't have you. First off, they're a risk. But what's more is I think, that I'll admit, I have a bias. I think we are better people than those who go out and hurt kids.
<v Adam>有一次有人进来了，他几乎立刻向我承认，他曾对一个5岁的孩子做过一些性行为。当场我就说我们不能要你。首先，他们是个风险。但更重要的是，我承认，我有偏见。我认为我们比那些去伤害孩子的人更好。

00:51:42.720 --> 00:51:45.270
<v Luke Malone>Did you tell him that?
<v Luke Malone>你告诉他了吗？

00:51:45.270 --> 00:52:00.390
<v Adam>I explained to him, you know, to the best of my ability, that what he did was very wrong. And that the most noble thing he could possibly do would be to tell the kid's parents so that at least that kid could get the help he might need.
<v Adam>我尽我所能向他解释说，他所做的事是非常错误的。而且他能做的最高尚的事就是告诉孩子的父母，以便那个孩子至少能得到他可能需要的帮助。

00:52:00.390 --> 00:52:03.800
<v Luke Malone>And what was his response?
<v Luke Malone>他的反应是什么？

00:52:03.800 --> 00:52:05.280
<v Adam>Something like maybe.
<v Adam>大概是“也许吧”之类的话。

00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:23.340
<v Luke Malone>In a different world, this person would be talking to a professional, not a 19-year-old with no training at all. Or maybe this person would just be in prison.
<v Luke Malone>在另一个世界里，这个人会和专业人士交谈，而不是一个毫无训练的19岁年轻人。或者，也许这个人就应该呆在监狱里。

00:52:23.340 --> 00:52:46.380
<v Luke Malone>Here's another important distinction. Eight out of the nine in Adam's group say they are nonexclusive pedophiles, which means they are also attracted to their peers or adults, in addition to kids. That's important because researchers like Elizabeth Letourneau think it might be possible to push people like that to become more attracted to people their own age, if you start young.
<v Luke Malone>这是另一个重要的区别。亚当小组的9个人中有8个说他们是非排他性恋童癖者，这意味着除了孩子之外，他们也受同龄人或成年人吸引。这很重要，因为像伊丽莎白·勒图诺这样的研究人员认为，如果你从年轻时就开始干预，可能有可能推动像这样的人变得对同龄人产生更多吸引力。

00:52:46.380 --> 00:53:02.090
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>Yeah, so through hanging out with peers more often, engaging in fun things with peers more often, really increasing that, I really believe, at least for some kids, some portion of kids who are sexually attracted to children, it's changeable. I don't want to start with the premise that it's impossible.
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>是的，所以通过更频繁地与同龄人一起相处，更频繁地与同龄人一起进行有趣的活动，真正增加这一点，我真的相信，至少对一些孩子，对某些受儿童性吸引的孩子来说，这是可以改变的。我不想从“这是不可能的”这个前提开始。

00:53:02.090 --> 00:53:29.870
<v Luke Malone>When I first started talking to Letourneau a year and a half ago, she told me that in her 25 years in the field, she'd talked to lots of young guys who've abused children. But she'd never spoken to a pedophile who hasn't, which I found pretty incredible. I told her about Adam's group, and she asked if I could put them in touch. She's since spoken to several of them and has been talking to Adam regularly. And she's started to notice patterns, pattens that she can use to inform a treatment plan that she's getting off the ground.
<v Luke Malone>当我一年半前第一次开始和勒图诺交谈时，她告诉我，在她25年的领域工作中，她和许多虐待过儿童的年轻人谈过话。但她从未和没虐待过儿童的恋童癖者交谈过，这让我觉得很不可思议。我告诉她亚当的小组，她问我能否联系上他们。此后她和他们中的几个人谈过，并一直在定期和亚当交流。她开始注意到一些模式，这些模式可以用来为她正在开展的治疗方案提供信息。

00:53:29.870 --> 00:53:46.030
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>You know, before talking to Adam and the other young men, I didn't know when it really crystallized for them that this wasn't going away. I didn't know what the experiences were. I had no idea about the deep depression and the self-loathing and the fear that really characterized all of their adolescence.
<v Elizabeth Letourneau>你知道，在和亚当以及其他年轻人交谈之前，我不知道他们何时真正明确了这种吸引力不会消失。我不知道他们的经历是什么。我根本不知道深层的抑郁、自我厌恶和恐惧，这些确实是他们所有青春期的特征。

00:53:46.030 --> 00:54:01.020
<v Luke Malone>While Letourneau is just starting to learn about what causes pedophilia and develop methods for treatment, Adam doesn't agree that he can be fixed. He doesn't hold out hope for the possibility of becoming something other than a pedophile. It took him years to figure it out in the first place.
<v Luke Malone>虽然勒图诺才刚刚开始了解导致恋童癖的原因并制定治疗方法，但亚当不同意他能被“治愈”。他不抱希望自己能变成恋童癖以外的人。他花了好几年才首先搞清楚这一点。

00:54:01.020 --> 00:54:12.700
<v Adam>The truth is, I know what my attractions are. I know they're there. By every definition of the medical term, I am one. Sometimes, you really just know these things.
<v Adam>事实是，我知道我的吸引力是什么。我知道它们在那里。根据医学术语的每一个定义，我就是其中之一。有时，你确实就是知道这些事情。

00:54:12.700 --> 00:54:23.440
<v Luke Malone>Adam says being a pedophile is something he'll spend the rest of his life battling. But he's committed to managing it. He's thought ahead to his future in a way that most 19-year-olds don't.
<v Luke Malone>亚当说，作为一名恋童癖者是他余生都要战斗的事情。但他致力于管理它。他以大多数19岁年轻人不会有的方式预想了自己的未来。

00:54:23.440 --> 00:54:57.450
<v Adam>You know, I'd like a partner, obviously. The thought of having a kid is very scary. I'm not convinced I could ever allow myself to do that, as much as I may want it. I think, most people want kids at some point in their lives. And that's something that while I'm not saying I never will have, it's something I don't think I will have, I guess, for both of our safeties.
<v Adam>你知道，我显然想要个伴侣。想要个孩子的想法非常可怕。我不相信我能允许自己那样做，尽管我可能很想要。我想，大多数人在生命的某个阶段都想要孩子。而那件事，虽然我不是说我永远不会有，但我认为我不会拥有，我想，这是为了我们双方的安全。

00:54:57.450 --> 00:55:23.930
<v Luke Malone>Imagine being a teenager and being told never to act on your sexual feelings ever for the rest of your life. That's what we're asking of these people. At the moment, there is no clear plan for how to do that. But maybe there should be.
<v Luke Malone>想象一下作为一个青少年，被告知余生都绝不能根据你的性感受去行动。这就是我们对这些人提出的要求。目前，没有明确的计划来执行这一点。但也许应该有。

00:55:23.930 --> 00:55:31.080
<v Ira Glass>Luke Malone. More of his reporting on this topic will appear next month on Medium.com.
<v Ira Glass>卢克·马龙。他关于这一主题的更多报道将于下个月出现在Medium.com上。

